  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d01fd2d64a9249049aaa77d5c12a82fe, type: 3}
  m_Name: Question 7
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  questionText: 7. Positions of the main scale and circular scale of a screw gauge
    are shown here when the screw of a screw gauge touches the stud. The least count
    of the screw gauge is 0.01 mm. The zero error of the screw gauge is
  referenceImage: {fileID: 0}
  explanationText: 'If the zero of the circular scale lies below the zero of the
    main scale when the end of the screw and surface of the stud are brought in contact
    with each other, the error is called the positive zero error.

    Zero error
    = (Coinciding circular scale division with the main scale) x Least count

    Zero
    error = 2 x 0.01 mm

    Zero error = 0.02 mm'
  options:
  - '-0.02 mm '
  - '-0.004 mm  '
  - '0.02 mm  '
  - 0.04 mm
  correctOptionIndex: 2
